{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And there shall be darkness.</b> This is an expression of removal, for by the nature of creation every person has day and also night. What did the Holy One, blessed be He, do? He removed the plain darkness of night from the boundary of Israel and placed it upon the land of Egypt, and therefore Egypt had doubled darkness. And for this reason even by day 'the wicked are silenced in darkness' (I Samuel 2:9), for the sun had no time to shine except by day, since the night is in any case dark. And for this reason the children of Israel had light in their dwellings even at night. A hint to the matter: 'וּלְכָל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל הָיָה' (Exodus 10:23) — these four words, their final letters spell לַיְלָה ('night'), and afterward it is written 'אוֹר בְּמוֹשְׁבֹתָם' ('light in their dwellings'), as if to say that even at night there was light for Israel, as it is written (Psalms 139:11) 'וְלַיְלָה אוֹר בַּעֲדֵנִי' ('but the night is light about me'). And this is what Rashi said, that the darkness was doubled — that is, by the measure of both day and night.'" "And as for what Rashi asks — why did He bring darkness upon them? And Rashi did not ask thus concerning all the plagues — because in all those plagues, if Pharaoh wished to repent while the plague was still in force, he was able. But here, 'no man rose from his place' (Exodus 10:23) for all three days, and even if he had wanted to repent during the three days he could not have — so why should such a thing go forth from before Him, blessed be He? For even though HaShem had already hardened his heart, that was because he himself had hardened his own heart while the plague was still in force; therefore it is just to harden his heart after the plague's removal. But with the plague of darkness, even if he had wanted to repent while the plague was in force he could not have — so why did HaShem bring this plague, to withhold from him the path of repentance? Rather, it was because of the wicked of Israel, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:14.745983734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}